  "limits": [
    "No live YouTube visit, failing user session or production ad payload was tested. Offline results establish mechanics and safeguards, not universal live ad coverage or anti-detection.",
    "Page-world registrations remain at document_start. Retained IDs are updated in place; obsolete IDs alone are removed. Existing page hooks require a page reload after changing protection or updating the extension.",
    "Player filtering is bounded to 512 queued objects, 4096 properties and eight levels. Same-origin player/next text filtering is limited to 4 MiB. Alternate/captured transports, raw JSON.parse reviver observation, locked globals and stitched ads may bypass it.",
    "Fallback waits for verified policy and positive ad classes. Unknown or incompletely seekable media is not sought; newer sound/speed edits survive restoration. At most 32 media states are retained, with cleanup on disable, detach and trusted navigation.",
    "Disposable package aliases enable YouTube policy only on the owned loopback route; original and modified hashes are separate. Silent PCM media is generated locally. Non-loopback browser traffic is denied.",
    "The initial regression run had six failures on the old implementation. After the fix, four tests failed only because registration ordering is no longer canonical; assertions now compare ID-sorted registration contents.",
    "The first two Edge fixture runs lacked media byte-range support, so the safety guard correctly refused an unseekable end. The third expected the old rate after native load() reset it. The fixture now serves byte ranges and establishes the baseline after reset; all criteria pass without relaxing the guards."
  ],
